repository-code: "https://github.com/souravmb/epa-tri-ensemble-regression"

type: software

version: "1.0.0"

date-released: "2025-01-01"

license: MIT

abstract: >-
  A rigorously leak-guarded machine learning pipeline for
  predicting total toxic chemical releases (in pounds) using
  the EPA Toxics Release Inventory 2022 dataset (80,040
  facility-chemical records, 122 variables). Implements five
  regression models, Bayesian hyperparameter optimisation via
  Optuna TPE, and a two-level stacking ensemble combining
  Differential Evolution-optimised weighted blending with a
  Linear Regression meta-learner. Final ensemble achieves
  RMSE = 0.2341 and R² = 0.9966 on the log-transformed target.
  SHAP TreeExplainer analysis provides model interpretability.
  Built as a Marimo reactive notebook for full reproducibility.

keywords:
  - EPA TRI
  - Toxics Release Inventory
  - ensemble learning
  - gradient boosting
  - XGBoost
  - differential evolution
  - Bayesian optimisation
  - Optuna
  - SHAP
  - data leakage prevention
  - environmental data science
  - Marimo
  - machine learning
  - regulatory prediction

references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "EPA TRI Basic Data Files — Calendar Years 1987–Present"
    url: "https://www.epa.gov/toxics-release-inventory-tri-program/tri-basic-data-files-calendar-years-1987-present"
    authors:
      - name: "U.S. Environmental Protection Agency"
